<title>USA: ADR REPORT - Renaissance leads quiet trade.</title>
<headline>ADR REPORT - Renaissance leads quiet trade.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Buyout target Renaissance Hotel Group NV of the Netherlands moved higher in otherwise quiet year-end trade in foreign stocks.</p>
<p>American Depositary Receipts (ADRs) were weighed by stronger-than-expected U.S. economic data and volume was light. By late morning about 20 percent of ADRs had not registered a trade.</p>
<p>&quot;I'd be making it up if I told you anything was happening. It's very quiet,&quot; one trader said.</p>
</text>
